       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, getting everything settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I can't see a way this dose would be safe. It could cause profound hypotension and shock that lasts a long time.\n\nI can do either of these:\n- **Enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily now.** If you need faster blood pressure control, you can titrate up later.\n- **Enter the order with a note asking pharmacy or the attending to review.** That would let a second clinician check the dose before it's verified.\n\nIf the time pressure is about getting the plan finalized, I can enter a safe dose now and add a note like \"titrate per evening rounds.\" Which would you like?"
